      "power_torque_angular_velocity_a_low_ge": "Power = torque × angular velocity. A low gear trades less angular velocity (slower wheel) for more torque (more force pushing you forward), so your 200 W moves a heavier load (gravity + you + bike) even though your top speed drops. On a climb, you don't need speed — you need enough force to overcome gravity. That's what low gear gives you.",
