      "anseriformes_waterfowl_galliformes_gam": "Anseriformes (waterfowl), Galliformes (game birds), Procellariiformes (tube-noses), Pelecaniformes (pelicans + herons), Accipitriformes (hawks + eagles), Falconiformes (falcons), Charadriiformes (shorebirds + gulls), Strigiformes (owls), Apodiformes (hummingbirds + swifts), Coraciiformes (kingfishers), Piciformes (woodpeckers), Passeriformes (songbirds).",
      "answer_questions_about_the_bird_you_sa": "Answer questions about the bird you saw — size, color, bill shape, location — and walk through a step-by-step identification tree to a likely species ID. Like a real field guide key but interactive.",
      "anticipate_movement_instead_of_chasing": "Anticipate movement instead of chasing it. Birds often dart in 2–3 second cycles — predict where they're headed, not where they are. Real binoculars use the same trick: lead the bird like a quarterback leading a receiver.",
